%description:

Tcp.windowScalingFactor:auto-boundary-synack -- the SYN-ACK of a passive opener one byte above the largest window of a shift count announces the next shift count.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "-1 for automatic selection: the smallest shift count that represents
the largest window that the connection can offer, advertisedWindow [...]".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), explicit (0 to 14), invalid (below -1 or above 14),
too-small (a factor that cannot represent advertisedWindow). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks the value, and the options of the SYN select
the factor. This test separates "auto" from "explicit".

The facet auto-boundary: the largest window of the shift count 1 is 65535 << 1 = 131070 bytes,
so a window of 131071 bytes needs the shift count 2. A selection that shifts the window down
with truncation gives 1 (131071 >> 1 = 65535), and the connection cannot offer its last byte.
The facet auto-boundary-synack checks the passive opener, which selects its shift count when
it answers the SYN.

Host under test: host2, which listens at the port 1000, with advertisedWindow = 131071 (a
precondition); host1 opens the connection with the defaults. Observation: level 1, the Window
Scale option of the SYN-ACK of host2 has the shift count 2.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# class: auto-boundary-synack
%# value: -1
%# key: *.host2.tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpWindowScalingFactorAutoBoundarySynAck")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpWindowScaleOptionOf(context.event.packet) == 2; })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2, with the shift count 2")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowScalingFactorAutoBoundarySynAck compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.windowScalingFactor = -1    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 131071
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpWindowScalingFactorAutoBoundarySynAck: PASS
